From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:26:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): offer a jump to the latest message with a
 new-reply signal

A reader who scrolls up in the transcript releases follow-tail and then has
no labelled way back and no sign that the conversation moved on below them.
The stock ConversationScrollButton rendered an unlabeled arrow 16px inside
the scroll container, inside the 32px scroll fade, with no notification
state and no accessible name.

Replace it with a bottom-edge pill mounted into the conversation wrapper
(outside the fade) that reads the StickToBottom context: "Jump to latest"
while the reader is away from the bottom, "New reply" while a turn streams
below them, "N new messages" once distinct user/assistant messages have
been appended since the last one they saw at the bottom (older history
paged in above does not count). The notification state uses the filled
primary button; the idle state matches the Jump-to-top pill. Clicking
scrolls to the bottom and re-arms follow-tail. The pill is keyboard
reachable with an aria-label that carries the count, always visible while
away on desktop and touch alike, and appears only after a short settle so
the mount pin and deep-link scrolls never flash it.

The counting and labelling are pure helpers with unit tests; the pill is
tested inside the real Conversation context with a simulated scroll-away.

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/transcript-jump-to-latest; drop this copy
once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit f0bb4c17c732d0b7257a2f8eaab2573c454c33af)
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Docs: none (transcript control that appears by itself when you scroll up; no setting)
